/* book Worked example: Q: Estimate the diffusivity of CO2 in air at 300 K and 1 atm with the Fuller correlation. Data: M of CO2 = 44 g/mol, M of air = 29 g/mol, diffusion volume increments Σv = 26.9 for CO2 and 20.1 for air.
   1. Correlation with P in atm gives D in cm²/s: DAB = 1.00×10⁻³ T1.75 (1/MA + 1/MB)0.5 / [P (ΣvA1/3 + ΣvB1/3)²].
   2. Mass term: (1/44 + 1/29)0.5 = (0.05721)0.5 = 0.2392. Temperature term: 3001.75 = 2.163×10⁴.
   3. Volume term: 26.91/3 = 3.00 and 20.11/3 = 2.72; (3.00 + 2.72)² = 32.7.
   4. DAB = 1.00×10⁻³ × 2.163×10⁴ × 0.2392/(1 × 32.7) = 0.158 cm²/s = 1.58×10⁻⁵ m²/s.
   Answer: DAB for CO2 in air at 300 K and 1 atm is about 0.158 cm²/s, that is 1.58×10⁻⁵ m²/s. */
